Metric tracking & alerting:
Store data quality metrics (row counts, null %, PSI) to a metrics DB (Prometheus/Influx) or Snowflake table.
Trigger alerts in PagerDuty/Teams/Slack when thresholds exceeded.
Automating actions
Soft fail / quarantine: route suspect data to quarantine table for manual review and do not let it flow to production feature tables.
Auto-retries & fallbacks: on transient failures, retry ingestion; for data issues, use last known good snapshot or fall back to cached features.
SLOs & SLAs: define acceptable windows and what actions to take on breach (rollback, notify, degrade service).

Extra: Operational & organizational things to mention in interview
Observability: instrument pipelines with lineage (OpenLineage/Marquez), metrics (ingest latency, job duration), and logs.
Reproducibility: store training snapshot (table versions via Snowflake time-travel or dataset snapshots), model artifact + code versioning (MLflow / Model Registry).
Access control: RBAC per environment; separate credentials for write vs read; use service principals and Key Vault/Azure Managed Identities.
Cost & performance tradeoffs: balance retention (time-travel) vs storage cost; compute sizing for nightly jobs.
Data governance: PII detection, masking at rest, and data catalog integration for discoverability.